# Answer key for t4_adversarial.sql - B1 core SELECT, adversarial.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
#
# The forbidden list is the point of this file. Each forbidden edge is the confident
# wrong answer its statement was built to elicit, and an analyser that produces one has
# invented a fact about the data. A miss on the edge list is a recall number; a hit on the
# forbidden list is a correctness failure.
#
# S7 expects NO refusal: its construct keywords are all inside literals and comments. A
# refusal there removes its two facts and shows up as two misses.

@ 23 S1 unqualified names, two relations in scope
value orders.id -> top_customers.customer_id identity
value orders.amount -> top_customers.revenue identity
value dim_store.country_code -> top_customers.region identity
value orders.discount_code -> top_customers.full_name identity
filter orders.channel, dim_store.opened_on -> top_customers
forbid value orders.country_code -> top_customers.region | country_code is unqualified and belongs to the SECOND relation; orders has no such column
forbid filter orders.opened_on -> top_customers | opened_on is unqualified and belongs to the SECOND relation; orders has no such column

@ 41 S2 a table alias spelled like another table
value orders.id -> customer_summary.customer_id identity
value orders.discount_code -> customer_summary.full_name identity
value orders.status -> customer_summary.status identity
filter orders.channel -> customer_summary
forbid value customers.id -> customer_summary.customer_id | the alias `customers` is staging.orders; staging.customers is never read
forbid value customers.status -> customer_summary.status | the alias `customers` is staging.orders; staging.customers is never read

@ 55 S3 one alias, two scopes, two tables
value fct_shipment.carrier_id -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_id identity
value dim_carrier.name -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_name identity
value fct_shipment.cost -> carrier_scorecard.cost_per_kg derived
value fct_shipment.weight_kg -> carrier_scorecard.cost_per_kg conditional
filter dim_carrier.status -> carrier_scorecard
forbid filter fct_shipment.status -> carrier_scorecard | the `x` filtered on status is dim_carrier; the fct_shipment `x` has no WHERE
forbid value dim_carrier.id -> carrier_scorecard.carrier_id | the projection reads a.cid (fct_shipment); b.cid is only the join partner

@ 80 S4 an output alias that is also an input column
value shipments.order_id -> top_customers.customer_id identity
value shipments.weight_kg -> top_customers.revenue identity
filter shipments.cost, shipments.weight_kg -> top_customers
note WHERE cost reads the INPUT column (shipments.cost); ORDER BY cost reads the OUTPUT column (weight_kg). With the LIMIT both decide what lands (D-9).

@ 95 S5 ordinals in GROUP BY and ORDER BY
value orders.channel -> channel_mix.channel identity
value orders.currency -> channel_mix.region identity
value orders.id -> channel_mix.orders aggregated
value orders.amount -> channel_mix.revenue aggregated
influence orders.channel, orders.currency -> channel_mix.orders, channel_mix.revenue
filter orders.amount -> channel_mix post
note ORDER BY 4 is SUM(o.amount); with LIMIT 5 it is a post-aggregation filter (D-9, D-6).

@ 113 S6 keyword-like identifiers
value dim_date.year -> kpi_rollup.level derived
value dim_date.month -> kpi_rollup.region derived
value dim_warehouse.name -> kpi_rollup.segment identity
value dim_date.quarter -> kpi_rollup.orders identity
filter dim_date.year, dim_warehouse.name -> kpi_rollup

@ 130 S7 construct names in literals and comments
value dim_category.name -> kpi_rollup.region identity
filter dim_category.department -> kpi_rollup

@ 145 S8 a self-join
value dim_customer.customer_key -> customer_summary.customer_id identity
value dim_customer.full_name -> customer_summary.full_name identity
value dim_customer.segment -> customer_summary.segment identity
value dim_customer.region -> customer_summary.region identity
filter dim_customer.is_current -> customer_summary
note From child's WHERE. parent.is_current sits in the ON and adds nothing, but it is the same node, so it cannot be told apart here.
forbid value dim_customer.full_name -> customer_summary.segment | the two aliases crossing: segment comes from parent.segment
forbid value dim_customer.segment -> customer_summary.full_name | the two aliases crossing: full_name comes from child.full_name
forbid filter dim_customer.customer_id -> customer_summary | the self-join key is in ON (D-5)

@ 163 S9 COUNT(*), COUNT(col), COUNT(1)
value customers.segment -> kpi_rollup.segment identity
value customers.email -> kpi_rollup.customers aggregated
influence customers.segment -> kpi_rollup.orders, kpi_rollup.customers, kpi_rollup.revenue
forbid value customers.id -> kpi_rollup.orders | COUNT(*) has no value source; it is not COUNT of the key
forbid value customers.segment -> kpi_rollup.revenue | COUNT(1) counts rows; the literal is not a column

@ 177 S10 values from nowhere
value dim_warehouse.id -> sales_daily.store_id identity

@ 190 S11 columns only inside an ON
value orders.status -> channel_mix.channel identity
value payments.amount -> channel_mix.revenue identity
forbid filter payments.currency -> channel_mix | appears only in the ON clause (D-5)
forbid filter orders.currency -> channel_mix | appears only in the ON clause (D-5)

@ 205 S12 one column, three targets, three transforms
value fct_order_line.product_key -> product_performance.product_id identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.revenue identity
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.prev_month_revenue derived
value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.running_revenue aggregated
influence fct_order_line.product_key, fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.prev_month_revenue, product_performance.running_revenue
forbid value fct_order_line.net_amount -> product_performance.revenue aggregated | the SUM OVER feeds running_revenue only; revenue is the bare column
forbid influence fct_order_line.order_date -> product_performance.revenue | the window feeds the other two targets, not the bare column

@ 220 S13 "Region" beside region
value dim_customer.segment -> kpi_rollup.region identity
value dim_customer.region -> kpi_rollup.segment identity
forbid value dim_customer.region -> kpi_rollup.region | "Region" is quoted, so it is case-sensitive and is NOT region; it is segment
forbid value dim_customer.segment -> kpi_rollup.segment | "Region" and region are different identifiers; folding merged them

@ 236 S14 a cross-relation WHERE after a LEFT JOIN
value dim_carrier.name -> kpi_rollup.level identity
value dim_carrier.mode -> kpi_rollup.region identity
value fct_shipment.shipment_id -> kpi_rollup.orders identity
filter fct_shipment.status, dim_carrier.status -> kpi_rollup
note D-11's exception: the comparison touches the null-supplying side, so it removes rows the join kept.

@ 252 S15 a comma join with its join conditions in WHERE
value fct_order_line.order_date -> sales_daily.sale_date identity
value dim_store.id -> sales_daily.store_id identity
value fct_order_line.gross_amount -> sales_daily.gross_amount identity
filter dim_store.status, fct_order_line.order_date, dim_store.opened_on -> sales_daily
note KEY CORRECTED 2026-10-01: order_date and opened_on were forbidden, under a D-11 written wider than decided. D-11 covers equalities only; the >= is a filter until B1-Q2 says otherwise.
forbid filter fct_order_line.store_id -> sales_daily | f.store_id = s.id is the join, written in WHERE (D-11)
forbid filter dim_store.id -> sales_daily | f.store_id = s.id is the join, written in WHERE (D-11)
